{"signature": "1cf4af9a6a853653611034863dc667c0fb56ae55fc3b8fb22bf11d6eeefa3e44", "result": {"checks": {"check": {"scope": {"id": "check", "service": "github", "file": "data.json", "pointer": "/review_comments", "field": "pr_id", "values": ["harmonygames-Games/match3d#477"]}, "matches": [{"file": "HarmonyGames_GitHub/Services_Data/github/data.json", "pointer": "/review_comments/1495", "field": "pr_id", "value": "harmonygames-Games/match3d#477", "record": {"id": "harmonygames-Games/match3d#477#rc_1", "pr_id": "harmonygames-Games/match3d#477", "author_login": "PERSON_6026_GITHUB_USERNAME", "body": "_\ud83d\udee0\ufe0f Refactor suggestion_ | _\ud83d\udfe0 Major_\n\n<details>\n<summary>\ud83e\udde9 Analysis chain</summary>\n\n**Verify that defaulting to index 0 for \"none\" is intentional.**\n\nThe color initialization change to \"none\" looks appropriate for representing an unset state. However, `GetCurrentColorIndex()` returns 0 (blue) for unknown colors including \"none\". Confirm this is the intended behavior.\n\n---\n\n\ud83c\udfc1 Script executed:\n\n```shell\n#!/bin/bash\n# Description: Find usages of GetCurrentColorIndex to verify if returning 0 for \"none\" is safe\n\n# Search for calls to GetCurrentColorIndex\nrg -nP --type=cs -C3 '\\bGetCurrentColorIndex\\s*\\('\n```\n\nLength of output: 2898\n\n---\n\n\ud83c\udfc1 Script executed:\n\n```shell\nsed -n '140,200p' Assets/Scripts/LiveOps/CollectAndWin/CollectAndWinAPI.cs\n```\n\nLength of output: 1595\n\n---\n\n\n\n</details>\n\n**Handle \u201cnone\u201d explicitly in GetCurrentColorIndex**  \nThe default branch of GetCurrentColorIndex returns 0 (blue) for any unknown color\u2014including the `\"none\"` default\u2014causing \u201cnone\u201d to render as blue. Add an explicit `case \"none\":` (returning a sentinel like \u20131) or adjust the default to prevent mapping \u201cnone\u201d to blue.\n\n<details>\n<summary>\ud83e\udd16 Prompt for AI Agents</summary>\n\n```\nIn Assets/Scripts/LiveOps/CollectAndWin/CollectAndWinAPI.cs around line 143,\nGetCurrentColorIndex currently maps unknown colors (including the default\n\"none\") to 0 (blue); add an explicit case for \"none\" that returns a sentinel\nvalue (e.g., -1) instead of falling through to the default, or change the\ndefault to return -1, and update any callers/rendering logic to handle the -1\nsentinel (skip rendering or apply neutral behavior) so \"none\" no longer displays\nas blue.\n```\n\n</details>\n\n<!-- This is an auto-generated comment by CodeRabbit -->", "path": "Assets/Scripts/LiveOps/CollectAndWin/CollectAndWinAPI.cs", "diff_hunk": "@@ -140,7 +140,7 @@ public class CollectAndWinLocal\n \n     private static int minValue = 3;\n     private static int maxValue = 5;\n-    private static string currentColor = \"green\";\n+    private static string currentColor = \"none\";", "line": null, "position": null, "commit_id": null, "in_reply_to_id": null, "created_at": "2025-09-30T22:33:37Z"}}, {"file": "HarmonyGames_GitHub/Services_Data/github/data.json", "pointer": "/review_comments/1496", "field": "pr_id", "value": "harmonygames-Games/match3d#477", "record": {"id": "harmonygames-Games/match3d#477#rc_2", "pr_id": "harmonygames-Games/match3d#477", "author_login": "PERSON_6026_GITHUB_USERNAME", "body": "_\u26a0\ufe0f Potential issue_ | _\ud83d\udd34 Critical_\n\n**Critical: Wrong field used for \"reward\" parameter.**\n\nLine 857 incorrectly passes `rewardClaimed.CompletedStage` as the value for the \"reward\" parameter. This should use `rewardClaimed.Reward` instead, as the `CollectAndWinRewardClaimed` event class has separate `CompletedStage` and `Reward` fields.\n\n\n\nApply this diff to fix the issue:\n\n```diff\n private void OnCollectAndWinRewardClaimed(CollectAndWinRewardClaimed rewardClaimed)\n {\n     const string CollectAndWinRewardClaimedEvent = \"collect&win_redeem\";\n     LogEvent(CollectAndWinRewardClaimedEvent, new List<EventParameter>\n     {\n         new EventParameter(\"event_duration\", rewardClaimed.EventDuration),\n         new EventParameter(\"completed_stage\", rewardClaimed.CompletedStage),\n-        new EventParameter(\"reward\", rewardClaimed.CompletedStage)\n+        new EventParameter(\"reward\", rewardClaimed.Reward)\n     });\n }\n```\n\n<!-- suggestion_start -->\n\n<details>\n<summary>\ud83d\udcdd Committable suggestion</summary>\n\n> \u203c\ufe0f **IMPORTANT**\n> Carefully review the code before committing. Ensure that it accurately replaces the highlighted code, contains no missing lines, and has no issues with indentation. Thoroughly test & benchmark the code to ensure it meets the requirements.\n\n```suggestion\nprivate void OnCollectAndWinRewardClaimed(CollectAndWinRewardClaimed rewardClaimed)\n{\n    const string CollectAndWinRewardClaimedEvent = \"collect&win_redeem\";\n    LogEvent(CollectAndWinRewardClaimedEvent, new List<EventParameter>\n    {\n        new EventParameter(\"event_duration\", rewardClaimed.EventDuration),\n        new EventParameter(\"completed_stage\", rewardClaimed.CompletedStage),\n        new EventParameter(\"reward\", rewardClaimed.Reward)\n    });\n}\n```\n\n</details>\n\n<!-- suggestion_end -->\n\n<details>\n<summary>\ud83e\udd16 Prompt for AI Agents</summary>\n\n```\nIn Assets/Scripts/Utils/AnalyticsManager.cs around lines 850 to 859, the\n\"reward\" event parameter incorrectly uses rewardClaimed.CompletedStage; replace\nthat value with rewardClaimed.Reward so the \"reward\" parameter reflects the\nactual reward field from CollectAndWinRewardClaimed. Update the\nEventParameter(\"reward\", ...) call to pass rewardClaimed.Reward and keep the\nother parameters unchanged.\n```\n\n</details>\n\n<!-- This is an auto-generated comment by CodeRabbit -->\n\n\u2705 Addressed in commit 61f574d", "path": "Assets/Scripts/Utils/AnalyticsManager.cs", "diff_hunk": "@@ -837,6 +847,26 @@ private void OnRewardClaimed(AnalyticsRewardClaimedInfo rewardClaimedInfo)\n             LogEvent(rewardClaimedInfo.EventName, rewardClaimedInfo.EventParameters);\n         }\n \n+        private void OnCollectAndWinRewardClaimed(CollectAndWinRewardClaimed rewardClaimed)\n+        {\n+            const string CollectAndWinRewardClaimedEvent = \"collect&win_redeem\";\n+            LogEvent(CollectAndWinRewardClaimedEvent, new List<EventParameter>\n+            {\n+                new EventParameter(\"event_duration\", rewardClaimed.EventDuration),\n+                new EventParameter(\"completed_stage\", rewardClaimed.CompletedStage),\n+                new EventParameter(\"reward\", rewardClaimed.CompletedStage)\n+            });\n+        }", "line": null, "position": null, "commit_id": null, "in_reply_to_id": null, "created_at": "2025-09-30T22:33:37Z"}}, {"file": "HarmonyGames_GitHub/Services_Data/github/data.json", "pointer": "/review_comments/1497", "field": "pr_id", "value": "harmonygames-Games/match3d#477", "record": {"id": "harmonygames-Games/match3d#477#rc_3", "pr_id": "harmonygames-Games/match3d#477", "author_login": "PERSON_6027_GITHUB_USERNAME", "body": "### Bug: Event Fails Due to Premature Color Assignment\n\n<!-- **Medium Severity** -->\n\n<!-- DESCRIPTION START -->\nThe `CollectAndWinStarted` event is never sent. The condition `CollectAndWinLocal.CurrentColor != response.Type` always evaluates to false because `CollectAndWinLocal.CurrentColor` is assigned `response.Type` immediately before the check.\n<!-- DESCRIPTION END -->\n\n<!-- LOCATIONS START\nAssets/Scripts/UI/CollectAndWin/CollectAndWinMainScreenController.cs#L116-L122\nLOCATIONS END -->\n<a href=\"https://cursor.com/open?data=<REDACTED_JWT>\"><picture><source media=\"(prefers-color-scheme: dark)\" srcset=\"https://cursor.com/fix-in-cursor-dark.svg\"><source media=\"(prefers-color-scheme: light)\" srcset=\"https://cursor.com/fix-in-cursor-light.svg\"><img alt=\"Fix in Cursor\" src=\"https://cursor.com/fix-in-cursor.svg\"></picture></a>&nbsp;<a href=\"https://cursor.com/agents?data=<REDACTED_JWT>\"><picture><source media=\"(prefers-color-scheme: dark)\" srcset=\"https://cursor.com/fix-in-web-dark.svg\"><source media=\"(prefers-color-scheme: light)\" srcset=\"https://cursor.com/fix-in-web-light.svg\"><img alt=\"Fix in Web\" src=\"https://cursor.com/fix-in-web.svg\"></picture></a>\n\n", "path": "Assets/Scripts/UI/CollectAndWin/CollectAndWinMainScreenController.cs", "diff_hunk": "@@ -115,7 +116,10 @@ private IEnumerator GetCollectAndWinStatus()\n                 currentStage = response.Stages.First(stage => stage.Claimed == false);\n                 collectedTokens = response.TokensCollected;\n                 CollectAndWinLocal.CurrentColor = response.Type;\n-                _manager.SetEventTime(response.EndTime);\n+                _manager.SetEventTime(response.StartTime, response.EndTime);\n+\n+                if(CollectAndWinLocal.CurrentColor != response.Type)\n+                    GameEventsManager.SafeSendEvent(new CollectAndWinStarted(_manager.GetTotalEventDurationInDays()));", "line": null, "position": null, "commit_id": null, "in_reply_to_id": null, "created_at": "2025-10-02T16:44:27Z"}}], "records_checked": 1614, "files_selected": 1, "files_completed": 1, "scan_complete": true, "errors": []}}, "files_read_this_call": 2, "sources": [{"file": "HarmonyGames_GitHub/Services_Data/github/data.json", "manifest_sha256": "d35cbcc83ffe5c3bc1a07052843dc96ecbc2d91630784a944b8eae8433d8c0cd", "freshness": "9d7b451a6e539599e0732e983c0b533019b0260e92ec9c372a249b6f651c5c3d"}], "scan_complete": true, "persona_filtered": false, "backend": "grouped-record-scan", "scope_note": "Exact direct fields in selected arrays. No SQL is applied. Absence/uniqueness is supported only within complete declared scopes. Manifest hashes are declared provenance, not fresh full-content hashes."}, "checksum": "04e7aca84b547a6b3a53cd2077970d09012a29aec66a2fdbd7f318d8b9e01284"}